# W30b, host a (k10). First its own trip into dng205b1 and home by the gate disc: dng205b1's start.lua sets COUNTER 2
# (the dungeon, a session context value, 3.7) to 205 and the lobby keeps it, so the instance a hosts next has the context
# of a player who was in dng205, as b's. Then a hosts Dry Land and waits at stag0201's gate arrival until b's first
# arrival at dng205b2 is over, and goes on to dng205b2 through dng205b1. The ways on are the depart action with the
# exits' own targets (stag0202's matz01: dng205b1 point 0; dng205b1's matz02: dng205b2 point 0), a alone in its stage
# group. (No stay in the Dry Land dungeons: a k10 character fighting in dng205b1 died within 60 s in rounds r2b and r2c.
# The second way to Dry Land is the lobby gate's departure (stag0201 point 0) by depart: the gate action's menu, opened
# a second time, stood still in round r2f.)
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@110
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 1 until stage=stag0201,control
depart dng205b1 0 until stage=dng205b1,control
log a was in dng205
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control fail epoch>=@230
idle until frames>=120
depart stag0201 0 until stage=stag0201,control
log a hosts Dry Land
idle until epoch>=@280
depart dng205b1 0 until stage=dng205b1,control
log a in dng205b1
depart dng205b2 0 until stage=dng205b2,control
log a in dng205b2
idle until present=2,sealed>=600 or epoch>=@600
log b joined a in B2
